{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum","id":1389427,"title":"Dose Vampire Blood allow you to reduce your hunger below the BP Minimum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-17T13:04:58-07:00","id":1389427,"title":"Dose Vampire Blood allow you to reduce your hunger below the BP Minimum?","content":"Recently I stumbled over a Reddit thread with the advice, to reduce your hunger under the blood potency minimum hunger by drinking from other vampires. Which makes kind of sense, since older vampires are known for drinking from other Vampires to satisfy their hunger. But I can\u2019t find a paragraph about it in the V5 core, that specifically stated that. As I understand the rules, as they are written, only killing a human brings older vampires below the minimum hunger of the blood potency in question.<br /> <br /> What is right? Have I missed something? And if so, where is it to find in the book?<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:06:15-07:00","id":1389428,"title":"","content":"If you kill someone via diablerie, you'll reduce your Hunger to 0. Same as with a mortal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:12:18-07:00","id":1389431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1389428#post1389428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you kill someone via diablerie, you'll reduce your Hunger to 0. Same as with a mortal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, you actually did not. Page 211 in the Core book says: \u201cOnly draining a human of blood, thereby killing them, can reduce Hunger to 0.\u201d<br /> <br /> A \u201chuman\u201d!<br /> <br /> later in the part about the Blood Potency levels it is stautet about the same, with sometimes saying \u201chuman\u201d sometimes \u201cmortal\u201d. Even Diablerie seams unable to slack your hunger below the minimum. There is something about drinking from other vampires too, but it stated no exactions for vampiric blood, that would break the \u201cOnly (!!!) draining a human/mortal...\u201d-rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:14:55-07:00","id":1389433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1389431#post1389431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, you actually did not. Page 211 in the Core book says: \u201cOnly draining a human of blood, thereby killing them, can reduce Hunger to 0.\u201d<br /> <br /> A \u201chuman\u201d!<br /> <br /> later in the part about the Blood Potency levels it is stautet about the same, with sometimes saying \u201chuman\u201d sometimes \u201cmortal\u201d. Even Diablerie seams unable to slack your hunger below the minimum. There is something about drinking from other vampires too, but it stated no exactions for vampiric blood, that would break the \u201cOnly (!!!) draining a human/mortal...\u201d-rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Jason Carl had it do so in LA By Night.<br /> <br /> So it's been retconned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T13:25:02-07:00","id":1389437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1389433#post1389433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Jason Carl had it do so in LA By Night.<br /> <br /> So it's been retconned.</div> </div> </div> </div>makes sense. But it would also make sense if Vampire Blood would, at least, lower a Vampires Hunger a bit below the minimum. Was there any evidence for that in the show?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T19:56:23-07:00","id":1389542,"title":"","content":"Retconned in... a web series about White Wolf employees doing LARP? Is this going to make it into a printed book at some point to be an actual retcon rather than being someone's houserule in a completely different medium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T20:05:16-07:00","id":1389546,"title":"","content":"It sounds like one of those things they didn't clarify because it was so obvious. Of course diablerizing someone reduces your hunger to zero. If it didn't, that would be incredibly stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T00:43:34-07:00","id":1389585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1389546#post1389546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like one of those things they didn't clarify because it was so obvious. Of course diablerizing someone reduces your hunger to zero. If it didn't, that would be incredibly stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>maybe, yes, but you also could argue that vampires are already dead and it is not about the amount of blood but about killing and so on and so forth...<br /> <br /> But beside from the worst case (Diablerie) I think it would make sense if Vampire Blood would satisfy at least a bit more hunger then the BP-Minimum. Think about it, a Vampire with a minimum hunger of 3 has only 2 hunger left. That is not much, even with the rouse check 50/50 Chance and the discipline re-roll. It becomes arguable why old vampires are at the top, while they are unable to use their power properly. I always thought, at one point they start to drink from younger vampires (with all the associated risks) but that will just not happen if vampire blood provides no benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T06:39:31-07:00","id":1389652,"title":"","content":"maybe that means we can diablerize mortals now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T20:18:43-07:00","id":1391115,"title":"","content":"Diablerie to slake the final point of hunger seems like overkill. Virtually no player is going to diablerise just to do that, the penalties are just too high for a mechanic that you have to deal with all the time. A guaranteed loss of humanity every time you wanted to get your hunger to 0 is not a good trade-off.<br /> <br /> Drinking vampire blood is much riskier than human blood anyway. Nonconsensually doing it is difficult, and coming back to the same willing source will get you bloodbonded. Letting it slake the last point of hunger without killing would open an interesting risk/reward dynamic, rather than the &quot;bad idea on all accounts&quot; that it is now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T10:26:36-07:00","id":1391210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1389546#post1389546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like one of those things they didn't clarify because it was so obvious. Of course diablerizing someone reduces your hunger to zero. If it didn't, that would be incredibly stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cMust drain and kill a human to reduce Hunger below X\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> In what way does that make killing or draining a Vampire obvious? That reads as &quot;Only by doing activity Y can you achieve result Z.&quot; By RAW it must be a HUMAN.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T10:46:17-07:00","id":1391215,"title":"","content":"The issue is that the book is conspicuously silent on drinking supernatural blood to slake base hunger. The presence of the flaw Methuselah's Thirst confuses things even more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Flaw: (\u2022) Methuselah\u2019s Thirst. Your Hunger can only be fully slaked by the blood of supernatural creatures. (Alchemists may be able to thicken the Blood of thin-bloods enough to sate you.) Other-wise, it constantly remains at a minimum of 1. (Or higher, depending on Blood Potency (see p. 215). </div> </div> </div>What can be taken from this? Diablerie being a requirement to slake hunger is extremely crippling, and the mention of alchemists adds more questions. Is it referring to the &quot;defractionate&quot; alchemy, or something similar? That's done to blood bags.<br /> <br /> The wording here could imply anything from &quot;only diablerie can slake hunger&quot; to &quot;any supernatural blood, even if it is outside its host, can slake base hunger&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26181-malksam","name":"MalkSam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:23:55-07:00","id":1391228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391210#post1391210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u201cMust drain and kill a human to reduce Hunger below X\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> In what way does that make killing or draining a Vampire obvious? That reads as &quot;Only by doing activity Y can you achieve result Z.&quot; By RAW it must be a HUMAN.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because hunger 0 is achieved by feeding to the point of murder, and diablerie is murder-beyond-murder. Diablerie is literally digesting someone's soul like that Egyptian crocodile god. If devouring someone's life gets you to 0, devouring their soul should do it twice as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:18:47-07:00","id":1391282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391115#post1391115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie to slake the final point of hunger seems like overkill. Virtually no player is going to diablerise just to do that, the penalties are just too high for a mechanic that you have to deal with all the time. A guaranteed loss of humanity every time you wanted to get your hunger to 0 is not a good trade-off.<br /> <br /> Drinking vampire blood is much riskier than human blood anyway. Nonconsensually doing it is difficult, and coming back to the same willing source will get you bloodbonded. Letting it slake the last point of hunger without killing would open an interesting risk/reward dynamic, rather than the &quot;bad idea on all accounts&quot; that it is now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually to get bloodbonded in V5 you need to drink <b>directly</b> from the would be regnant. Here's the relevant passage:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V5 core rulebook, page 234</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as in the Embrace, the Blood consumed must be taken directly from the vein of the donor, as it loses its power to Bond in a matter of seconds unless drunk. The drinker must repeat the act on three separate nights with no more than a year between drinks for the Bond to fully form. (During their first year, a childe remains onethird of the way Bound to their sire, having already tasted their Blood once.) A regnant can have as many vampire thralls as they have dots of Blood Potency, and a thrall can only have one regnant, becoming immune to other Bonding attempts while Bound. If a regnant Bonds another thrall above their maximum Blood Potency limit, their oldest Bond with a thrall fades over the course of a week.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:59:09-07:00","id":1391426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391228#post1391228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because hunger 0 is achieved by feeding to the point of murder, and diablerie is murder-beyond-murder. Diablerie is literally digesting someone's soul like that Egyptian crocodile god. If devouring someone's life gets you to 0, devouring their soul should do it twice as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Only draining a human of blood, thereby killing them, can reduce Hunger to 0 .&quot; And the chart states that only &quot;Human Drained and killed&quot; is &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Only way to reach Hunger 0 (zero) &quot;<br /> <br /> You will please note murder is mentioned exactly 0 times while HUMAN is mentioned every time. While it would make sense for diablerie to result in Hunger zero that is explicitly not allowed by the the RAW. &quot;Only way&quot; means all other ways <b>do not have this result</b>, henceforth it is not &quot;obvious&quot; since by RAW it is specifically forbidden. This is actually pretty simple logic statements. That means you can't even &quot;Air Bud&quot; it like have 10 vampires feed to maximum non-harmful level (or one vampire multiple times) off of one human in the same scene. (Which doesn't make sense logically, but is not forbidden by RAW.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T05:58:44-07:00","id":1391465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391426#post1391426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><br /> You will please note murder is mentioned exactly 0 times while HUMAN is mentioned every time. While it would make sense for diablerie to result in Hunger zero that is explicitly not allowed by the the RAW. &quot;Only way&quot; means all other ways <b>do not have this result</b>, henceforth it is not &quot;obvious&quot; since by RAW it is specifically forbidden. This is actually pretty simple logic statements. That means you can't even &quot;Air Bud&quot; it like have 10 vampires feed to maximum non-harmful level (or one vampire multiple times) off of one human in the same scene. (Which doesn't make sense logically, but is not forbidden by RAW.)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Except on p.376 of the V5 core it speaks of even two vampires being able to get to hunger 0 by sucking dry a werewolf. So sure, you can go ahead and argue, that by RAW (which currently has five pages of rules errata) a single Vampire could not slake their hunger to 0 by drinking sucking dry a werewolf, because the text explicitly says two vampires who share the kill... but I'd go with the easy explanation and say that they did not plan this through or multiple people were writing the rules without checking what the other person wrote.<br /> <br /> Play whatever makes you happy. In my games, it's the killing of a victim that quells the beast, be the victim human, kindred or sentient other. The first two one-shots we played, we also had vampires being able to reduce their hunger to 0 just by feeding on other vampires. It highlighted themes of blood bonds, bloodsucker nests and the lures of diablerie. There was a Ventrue with a reasonably easy to fulfill prey exclusion of blood potency 3 regularly feeding vitae to his childer, to get them to hunger 0 without draining their herds and get shit done for him without screwing things up on his watch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T18:25:28-07:00","id":1391579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391465#post1391465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first two one-shots we played, we also had vampires being able to reduce their hunger to 0 just by feeding on other vampires. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would House Rule this that only higher BP Vitae allows the reduction of Hunger to 0. Diablerie would be required when feeding from those of a lower Blood Potency to reduce Hunger to 0. I think this plays in nicely with the Methuselahs are going to consume you when they wake. Just a thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:18:28-07:00","id":1391589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391465#post1391465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except on p.376 of the V5 core it speaks of even two vampires being able to get to hunger 0 by sucking dry a werewolf. So sure, you can go ahead and argue, that by RAW (which currently has five pages of rules errata) a single Vampire could not slake their hunger to 0 by drinking sucking dry a werewolf, because the text explicitly says two vampires who share the kill... but I'd go with the easy explanation and say that they did not plan this through or multiple people were writing the rules without checking what the other person wrote.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. V5 is written even worse than I initially thought. Maybe we need a V5.5 to have an actual system for feeding that is consistent, lol. <br /> <br /> My point was that &quot;A does not imply B.&quot; In fact A specifically implies not B. Therefore B is not a logical conclusion of A.<br /> <br /> Now we have C implies not A on page 376.<br /> A also implies not C.<br /> <br /> Which means either A is wrong, C is wrong or werewolves are actually 2 humans. Either way A nor C implies B.<br /> <br /> A= Only Human reducing vampires to hunger 0<br /> B= Diablerie reducing vampires to hunger 0<br /> C= Werewolves reducing 2 vampires to hunger 0<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T01:34:18-07:00","id":1391648,"title":"","content":"The act of diablerie itself will not reduce your hunger to 0. Draining the vampire victim to final death will do it. This was shown at least twice during L.A by Night. First when Victor killed a thin-blood drug dealer because his beast got the better of him. And second when X drained a gangrel but then decided to keep going.<br /> <br /> Considering Jason Carl is the story-teller for the series AND part of management at White Wolf and Paradox, I would say his allowing it can be considered canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:48:56-07:00","id":1391737,"title":"","content":"Should we be monitoring Jason Carl's Instagram and LinkedIn profiles to see what other canon revisions are being flung out into the ether in places that are likely unknown to the majority of people who've paid good money for this game? Maybe he posts song MIDI files about the subject on an old Myspace account too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:47:26-07:00","id":1391780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389427-dose-vampire-blood-allow-you-to-reduce-your-hunger-below-the-bp-minimum?p=1391648#post1391648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The act of diablerie itself will not reduce your hunger to 0. Draining the vampire victim to final death will do it. This was shown at least twice during L.A by Night. First when Victor killed a thin-blood drug dealer because his beast got the better of him. And second when X drained a gangrel but then decided to keep going.<br /> <br /> Considering Jason Carl is the story-teller for the series AND part of management at White Wolf and Paradox, I would say his allowing it can be considered canon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Jason Carl is a brand marketing manager, not a writer and as far as I know, not involved with mechanics initially (that was Karim and Kenneth).<br /> <br /> And all of LA by Night is filled with rules gaffes ,homebrew and ignored RAW.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't consider ANYTHING canon from it until it appears in a book.<br /> <br /> But that aside, every instance in the book requires KILLING to be the thing. Every instance we have of something slaking hunger to zero (such as the werewolf in the book), the act of killing is the important part. So by RAW, killing something by draining it to death (and for vampires, that is diablerie, because draining someone makes their Hunger to 5, which is not even torpor until they fail a rouse check that they can't avoid such as rising for the day) is the key. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:51:25-07:00","id":1391782,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Jason\u2019s a swell fellow, but L.A. by Night is not rules errata. They fudge rules and setting stuff for the sake of simplicity and drama. Which, you know, is fair enough, but we shouldn\u2019t be watching it for official rulings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}